---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import north from '../assets/atlas-experiment/north-painting.png';
import south from '../assets/atlas-experiment/south-input.png';

const [painted, guide] = await Promise.all([
  getImage({ src: north, width: 720, format: 'webp' }),
  getImage({ src: south, width: 1120, format: 'webp' }),
]);
---

<figure data-src={Astro.props['data-src']}>
  <svg class="desktop" viewBox="0 0 1000 475" role="img" aria-labelledby="atlas-handoff-title atlas-handoff-desc">
    <title id="atlas-handoff-title">The painted edge becomes part of the next tile’s input</title>
    <desc id="atlas-handoff-desc">On the left is the reviewed northern tile. Its bottom 129 pixels are outlined in gold. An arrow connects that strip to the top of the southern tile’s guide on the right. A second painted neighbour supplies the guide’s left edge. The river continues from the inherited strip into the blue route drawn on the guide.</desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="atlas-copy-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#d3a74e" />
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <text x="0" y="29">Reviewed northern tile</text>
    <text x="440" y="29">Guide for the tile below</text>
    <image href={painted.src} x="0" y="55" width="360" height="240" />
    <image href={guide.src} x="440" y="55" width="560" height="373.333" />
    <rect x="2" y="264.8" width="356" height="28.2" fill="none" stroke="#d3a74e" stroke-width="4" />
    <rect x="442" y="57" width="556" height="43" fill="none" stroke="#d3a74e" stroke-width="4" />
    <path d="M 361 280 H 394 V 79 H 435" fill="none" stroke="#d3a74e" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#atlas-copy-arrow)" />
    <text x="0" y="328" class="detail">Copy the bottom 129 pixels</text>
    <text x="440" y="460" class="detail">Painted neighbours + planned interior</text>
  </svg>
  <svg class="mobile" viewBox="0 0 560 935" role="img" aria-labelledby="atlas-mobile-title atlas-mobile-desc">
    <title id="atlas-mobile-title">Carry the painted edge into the next guide</title>
    <desc id="atlas-mobile-desc">The northern painting is above the southern guide. Gold outlines show the bottom 129 pixels copied from the painting to the top of the guide.</desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="atlas-mobile-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#d3a74e" />
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <text x="0" y="29">Reviewed northern tile</text>
    <image href={painted.src} x="0" y="55" width="560" height="373.333" />
    <rect x="2" y="381.3" width="556" height="45" fill="none" stroke="#d3a74e" stroke-width="4" />
    <text x="0" y="463" class="detail">Copy the bottom 129 pixels</text>
    <path d="M 548 432 V 507" fill="none" stroke="#d3a74e" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#atlas-mobile-arrow)" />
    <text x="0" y="500">Guide for the tile below</text>
    <image href={guide.src} x="0" y="520" width="560" height="373.333" />
    <rect x="2" y="522" width="556" height="43" fill="none" stroke="#d3a74e" stroke-width="4" />
    <text x="0" y="928" class="detail">Painted neighbours + planned interior</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>The gold outlines mark the same strip of the world. Its river, paths, trees and colour become the starting conditions for the next painting.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; overflow: visible; }
  text { font: 24px var(--font-ui); fill: var(--ink); }
  .detail { font-size: 22px; fill: var(--ink-muted); }
  .mobile { display: none; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .desktop { display: none; }
    .mobile { display: block; }
  }
</style>
